WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.280
Welcome to this 170th commencement ceremony of&nbsp;
Hillsdale College thank you for coming let us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.840
remember to be grateful for the blessings of the&nbsp;
Lord upon this college which have been abundant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:20.080
the ceremony is on the occasion of the graduation&nbsp;
of the seniors, but it's not just about them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.320
it took everybody here to produce this ceremony.&nbsp;
Take the faculty and the work they have done to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:35.920
lead us through the things we need to know because&nbsp;
of what we are. They live with the students,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:44.080
they laugh with them, they eat with them, they&nbsp;
cry with them. The parents are important this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.840
room is full of parents swelled with pride&nbsp;
they spend a third of their lives or more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.600
taking care of these young people and what they&nbsp;
give to their children is everything they've got.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:04.960
There are friends of the college here they support&nbsp;
the college everybody in this room and everybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.280
watching is part of the achievement&nbsp;
that we're here to celebrate today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.960
As a group and individually these seniors are the&nbsp;
best we ever had and I went back in my notes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:23.920
last year and verified that I said that last year&nbsp;
too and it was true both years and I expect it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:30.720
will be true next year you get a year to be top&nbsp;
of the heap but you are awesome people and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:37.760
will be greatly missed here except you are not&nbsp;
leaving after all you're going to live the life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:43.840
that you have prepared yourself to live and&nbsp;
you're going to live it in contact with this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:52.320
college which is a partnership that includes you.&nbsp;
You seniors new graduates you're at a pinnacle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.480
of sorts that's one metaphor pinnacle&nbsp;
another how about a crossroads&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.360
the metaphor works because you make a decision&nbsp;
you go one direction or another and there's an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:10.240
old blues idea that you meet the devil at the&nbsp;
crossroads at midnight and then you might ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:16.240
well why do you meet the devil at the crossroads&nbsp;
and the answer is most fundamentally because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.720
when you come to a place in your life where&nbsp;
you have to make a choice you aim up or down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:29.520
and so you know you're called upon to to&nbsp;
take the lessons that you've been taught in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:35.200
a university like this that that teaches you to&nbsp;
abide by the eternal verities to sacrifice your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.800
own narrow pretensions in the highest sense to&nbsp;
something that's truly better anything you pursue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:46.800
that isn't that is insufficient. You're a&nbsp;
particularized creature as a son of God or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.200
a daughter of God let's say you have something to&nbsp;
bring into the world that no one else can bring in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.320
and so if you fail in that duty&nbsp;
then you deprive the world of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.320
there's no shortage of suffering in life and&nbsp;
no one thinks their own suffering isn't real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.480
and maybe there's a possibility that&nbsp;
there's some aim that's so high that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:13.200
the attempt alone to move in that direction is&nbsp;
of sufficient value to act as a panacea for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.680
suffering and so you could say at the end of your&nbsp;
life oh my God that was so hard it was worth it

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.920
and so that's the choice you make at&nbsp;
the crossroads if you have any sense.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.840
Now at our freshman convocation, Dr.&nbsp;
Arnn told us to get your boots on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.480
we have to have this inherent desire&nbsp;
to learn and to expand our knowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:42.480
Hillsdale's given that to us. Here at Hillsdale&nbsp;
we are meant to be together as a family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:50.240
and more importantly we are meant to achieve&nbsp;
self-government together and along the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:58.160
you'll set down a path and live an example for&nbsp;
others to follow for the same end in other words&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.000
keep your boots on. I was&nbsp;
going to speak more extensively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.080
but Dr. Jordan Peterson covered most of&nbsp;
the topics I had planned to talk about

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:14.560
Actually I am here in my capacity my proud&nbsp;
capacity as chairman of the board of trustees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:20.480
of Hillsdale college and I'm representing the&nbsp;
board when I first of all thank the graduates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.200
for all they have brought to this campus over the&nbsp;
last several years you have not only received a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:31.920
world-class education you've learned what it takes&nbsp;
to be a good and effective citizen you spend time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.120
thinking about and talking about the good and&nbsp;
the true and the beautiful all that is inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.320
you now and it's just up to you to get out&nbsp;
